# Software

This is a list of software projects I am working on, or have worked on in the
past.

## CorA (Corpus Annotator)

CorA is a web-based annotation tool for word-level annotation of historical and
other non-standard language data, implemented in PHP and JavaScript with a MySQL
back-end. It was originally developed to annotate historical texts for the
[Anselm corpus][Anselm] and the
[reference corpus of Early New High German][ReF], but has since been used for a
variety of other projects, including the
[annotation of social media data][EmpiriST].

I am currently actively maintaining CorA as its main developer.

[<button class="button">Website</button>][CorA]
{:.button-container}

## Norma (Normalization Tool)

Norma is a tool for automatic spelling normalization of non-standard language
data. It was originally developed for use with historical documents in the
DFG-funded [Anselm project][Anselm].  Originally written by me in Python, it was
later ported to C++ (with optional bindings for Python 2.x) with the help of
[Florian Petran](http://www.linguistics.rub.de/~petran).

[<button class="button">Website</button>][Norma]
[<button class="button"><i class="fa fa-github"></i> GitHub repository</button>][Norma-GitHub]
{:.button-container}

## SimpleNLG for German

SimpleNLG for German is an adaption of the [SimpleNLG library][SimpleNLG] for
natural language generation, written in Java.  I created it as part of my
studies for my master's degree.

